{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"a91c59704092602e","name":"card_event_ambush","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/events/card_event_ambush","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FIERY AMBUSH","text":"Deal 3 damage to a unit. If the enemy now has no units, deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ.","flavorText":"In June 1944, as part of the preparations for the upcoming D-Day invasion, the Francs-tireurs et partisans (FTP), an armed resistance organization created by leaders of the French Communist Party, was actively engaged in sabotage and disrupting German supply lines. On that day, a convoy of German troops, including soldiers and vehicles, was passing through Tulle. The local Resistance fighters seized the opportunity and launched an ambush on the convoy. The ambush resulted in chaos and confusion among the German forces. The Resistance fighters targeted the vehicles, causing damage and casualties. They specifically focused on disabling the German tanks and armored vehicles, aiming to neutralize their firepower advantage. The surprise attack by the Resistance fighters caught the Germans off guard and delayed their progress. It also boosted the morale of the local population and inspired others to join the resistance movement. The Tulle ambush showcased the effectiveness of guerrilla tactics employed by the French Resistance, demonstrating their ability to strike at German forces and disrupt their operations. However, the German response to the ambush was brutal. In reprisal for the Resistance attack, the Germans carried out a series of severe reprisals, including the burning of the town of Tulle and the execution of numerous civilians. The reprisals served as a grim reminder of the risks faced by those involved in Resistance activities.","faction":"France","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_ambush","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_ambush_title","SourceString":"FIERY AMBUSH","LocalizedString":"FIERY AMBUSH"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_ambush_text","SourceString":"Deal 3 damage to a unit. If the enemy now has no units, deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ.","LocalizedString":"Deal 3 damage to a unit. If the enemy now has no units, deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_ambush_history","SourceString":"In June 1944, as part of the preparations for the upcoming D-Day invasion, the Francs-tireurs et partisans (FTP), an armed resistance organization created by leaders of the French Communist Party, was actively engaged in sabotage and disrupting German supply lines. On that day, a convoy of German troops, including soldiers and vehicles, was passing through Tulle. The local Resistance fighters seized the opportunity and launched an ambush on the convoy. The ambush resulted in chaos and confusion among the German forces. The Resistance fighters targeted the vehicles, causing damage and casualties. They specifically focused on disabling the German tanks and armored vehicles, aiming to neutralize their firepower advantage. The surprise attack by the Resistance fighters caught the Germans off guard and delayed their progress. It also boosted the morale of the local population and inspired others to join the resistance movement. The Tulle ambush showcased the effectiveness of guerrilla tactics employed by the French Resistance, demonstrating their ability to strike at German forces and disrupt their operations. However, the German response to the ambush was brutal. In reprisal for the Resistance attack, the Germans carried out a series of severe reprisals, including the burning of the town of Tulle and the execution of numerous civilians. The reprisals served as a grim reminder of the risks faced by those involved in Resistance activities.","LocalizedString":"In June 1944, as part of the preparations for the upcoming D-Day invasion, the Francs-tireurs et partisans (FTP), an armed resistance organization created by leaders of the French Communist Party, was actively engaged in sabotage and disrupting German supply lines. On that day, a convoy of German troops, including soldiers and vehicles, was passing through Tulle. The local Resistance fighters seized the opportunity and launched an ambush on the convoy. The ambush resulted in chaos and confusion among the German forces. The Resistance fighters targeted the vehicles, causing damage and casualties. They specifically focused on disabling the German tanks and armored vehicles, aiming to neutralize their firepower advantage. The surprise attack by the Resistance fighters caught the Germans off guard and delayed their progress. It also boosted the morale of the local population and inspired others to join the resistance movement. The Tulle ambush showcased the effectiveness of guerrilla tactics employed by the French Resistance, demonstrating their ability to strike at German forces and disrupt their operations. However, the German response to the ambush was brutal. In reprisal for the Resistance attack, the Germans carried out a series of severe reprisals, including the burning of the town of Tulle and the execution of numerous civilians. The reprisals served as a grim reminder of the risks faced by those involved in Resistance activities."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/France/Spring2023Candidates/t_resistance_fighter.t_resistance_fighter","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Look and Learn","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Historic